# Implementation Walkthrough: ZimaOS Setup Organization

The ZimaOS setup and configuration files have been successfully consolidated into the `d:\OS\Zimaos` directory, which is now the unified location for the `evatechnosoft/zimaSetup` repository contents.

## Changes Made

### File Consolidation
All key setup files were moved from `D:\OS` to `D:\OS\Zimaos`:
- **[zimasetup.md](file:///D:/OS/Zimaos/zimasetup.md)**: Unified internet and SSH setup command.
- **[setup.sh](file:///D:/OS/Zimaos/setup.sh)**: Core installation script.
- **[cloudflare_token.txt](file:///D:/OS/Zimaos/cloudflare_token.txt)**: Cloudflare tunnel token.
- **[daemon.json](file:///D:/OS/Zimaos/daemon.json)**: Docker DNS configuration.

### Git Configuration
- The files are now tracked within the git repository at `d:\OS\Zimaos`.
- Verified that the remote `origin` is correctly pointing to `https://github.com/evatechnosoft/zimaSetup.git`.

## Verification Results

### Directory Structure
```
D:\OS\Zimaos
├── .git/
├── cloudflare_token.txt
├── daemon.json
├── setup.sh
└── zimasetup.md
```

### Git Status
Run `git status` in `D:\OS\Zimaos` to see the updated tracking status. All previous setup files from the parent directory are now correctly placed and ready for version control.

## Future Use
Whenever you need to deploy or update ZimaOS, all necessary tools and documentation are now organized in a single dedicated folder.
